            "review_title": "Review at Mais Thai Cusine",
            "review_text": "Justin D\n7 contributions\n0\nTried almost everything. Some of the most authentic Thai food in Vietnam!\nFeb 2020\nIn the time I've lived in this city, I've seen Thai joints (other than Thai Market) come and go. This is the first one that feels like the kind of place you'd find in Chiang Mai, both in terms of the simple-but-not-ultra-bare-bones decor and the extensive menu. \n\nHer experience cooking in Thailand shows, too. I've tried most of the dishes on the menu and haven't really had a dud. If anything, maybe the pad Thai falls a little flat. But there are so many other dishes on the menu that are hard or impossible to find elsewhere in this city, e.g.:\n\n- Laab \n- Yum moo yor (Vietnamese sausage salad—yes, it's a Thai dish)\n- Kor moo yang (BBQ pork with tamarind sauce) or Gai yang (the chicken version)\n\nPlus there's always the standbys: som tam, pad see ew, pad krapow, regular ol' fried rice... I could go on forever. If you live here and you are craving Thai food like how it is in Thailand, you NEED to stop by.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten February 25, 2020",
